                <pb facs="0940" n="834" sameAs="frus:frus1906p1/pg834"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Minister Combs to the Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Guatemala</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1906-06-02"><hi rendition="#italic">June 2,
                        1906</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Combs says he has been requested by the Guatemalan minister for foreign
                    affairs to report that 250 armed men, of whose character he is not sure, entered
                    Guatemala from Salvador, but that no collision has yet taken place. Mr. Combs
                    has urged self-restraint in strong terms.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
